Moladah.Probably the same as Malatha, so often mentioned by Eusebius;
from whom it appears it was situated about twenty miles from
Hebron.

Antothite.This variation springs simply from the points; the word being
written [Anthôthîy ,] {Anethothite}
in Samuel, and here [Annethôwthîy ,]
{Antothite.}

Heled.Heleb seems evidently a mistake for Heled, which is
essentially the same with Heldai, the latter merely having a
paragogic [Yôwd,] {yood.}

Gershon.Gershon, [Gêrshôm ,] is called
[Gêreshown ,] Gershom, in the
parallel passage, simply by the mutation of [Nûwn,] {noon,}
into [Mêm,] {mem.}

